            <div xml:id="d156">

                <pb facs="0133" n="124" sameAs="frus:frus1940v02/pg124"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">340.1115A/830: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Kennedy</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-06-07T17:00:00+01:00">June 7, 1940—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received June 7—12:05 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1539. Your 1113, 6th. Thank you for the <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>.
                    It will take a big chunk out of our problem. We have plenty of people to fill
                    her, but many cannot pay the fares. We will use the $20,000 in accordance with
                    instructions contained in your 1015, 28th.</p>
                <p>I presume your references to unoccupied space concerns the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Acadia</hi> and <hi rendition="#italic">St. John</hi>.
                    We reported before that people simply would not travel on these ships. I cannot
                    say that I blame them. Every other vessel which left these shores, including
                    belligerent vessels, carried as many people as it was found practicable to put
                    on.</p>
                <p>We have warned all Americans still here that the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Washington</hi> may be their last opportunity for returning home and that
                    those who do not take advantage of this opportunity remain at their own
                    risk.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kennedy</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
